Subject: Cantor FPGA Lowering Profile Exploded Specification

Description: Derived SJS expansion for an optional future FPGA realization of eligible Cantor Process IR kernels. This profile defines eligibility, interface, evidence, admission, and software-to-hardware correspondence obligations while intentionally granting no HDL, HLS, synthesis, bitstream, board, or device implementation authority.

@ [exploded_uuid] e6369469-b967-487a-986c-e6f2fd9ba6e9
@ [processing_input_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_cantor_deterministic_runtime_activation\SJS_Processing_Input_Manifest.sop
@ [Simula_FPGA_correspondence] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Simula_Inference_Control_Correspondence_2026-08-05.sop
@ [process_exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Process_Procedure_Experiment.exploded.sop

& [ExplodedIdentity] is a non-executable target contract
  + [profile] is cantor-fpga-lowering-profile/0.1
  + [requirement_set] is CFLP-001 through CFLP-024
  + [authority_grade] is correspondence_contract_only
  + [authority_state] is unsigned_exploded_candidate

& [SemanticBoundaryRequirements] keep hardware below meaning
  + CFLP-001 SOP remains the authority for meaning, purpose, identity, constraints, and proof obligations
  + CFLP-002 Cantor Process Procedure remains the human and model-facing process language
  + CFLP-003 canonical Cantor Process IR is the only eligible semantic input to a future FPGA lowering path
  + CFLP-004 VHDL, Verilog, SystemVerilog, HLS C or C++, CIRCT, vendor IR, netlist, and bitstream are derived target artifacts and cannot redefine source semantics
  + CFLP-005 the profile cannot claim literal shared model hidden state, on-FPGA LLM inference, semantic truth, or model-quality improvement

& [KernelEligibilityRequirements] require bounded static behavior
  + CFLP-006 eligible kernels use finite fixed-width types, statically bounded collections, explicit process states, bounded event queues, and declared maximum steps
  + CFLP-007 eligible kernels are deterministic, effectless, free of recursion, dynamic allocation, operating-system calls, arbitrary code loading, and undeclared storage
  + CFLP-008 eligible candidates declare expected invocation frequency, latency, throughput, power, area, determinism, or isolation benefit and a software baseline
  + CFLP-009 profiling must identify a stable hot path before native-hardware lowering is authorized
  + CFLP-010 initial candidate families are digest or CRC pipelines, signed-catalogue lookup, bounded relation filtering, score accumulation, graph-frontier expansion, deterministic arbitration, FIFO messaging, barrier accounting, and trace emission
  + CFLP-011 model calls, semantic admission, policy judgment, explanation, filesystem, network, database, provider, calendar, Git, and external effects remain host-side

& [TwoRealizationRequirements] preserve interpreter and native options
  + CFLP-012 FPGA interpreter realization executes signed bounded Cantor bytecode or IR on a stable admitted circuit and treats procedures as data
  + CFLP-013 native realization synthesizes a stable admitted procedure or kernel into dedicated circuitry and requires a new target artifact identity
  + CFLP-014 a procedure admitted for software or interpreter execution is not thereby admitted for native hardware synthesis or device loading
  + CFLP-015 target selection must record device, board, toolchain, versions, constraints, interfaces, memory map, clocks, reset, and host protocol

& [InterfaceAndSchedulingRequirements] make the seam explicit
  + CFLP-016 host-device exchange uses typed versioned request, response, fault, control, and trace channels with exact schema and endianness
  + CFLP-017 process and message channels use bounded FIFO or equivalent handshake semantics with declared backpressure, fairness, deadlock, overflow, and reset behavior
  + CFLP-018 logical event order and deterministic tie-breaking must match the software reference independent of physical clock-cycle variation
  + CFLP-019 hardware resource exhaustion, timeout, reset, partial response, transport failure, and stale invocation produce typed fail-closed outcomes

& [CorrespondenceAndAdmissionRequirements] make hardware claims provable
  + CFLP-020 software reference and hardware candidate must consume identical normalized inputs and produce identical normalized typed results and semantic traces within declared cycle-only metadata exclusions
  + CFLP-021 verification must include IR validation, software golden tests, RTL or HLS simulation, property checks where applicable, synthesis evidence, timing closure, resource report, and target integration tests
  + CFLP-022 every compiler, IR, RTL, netlist, constraints, report, firmware, driver, and bitstream artifact binds digest, tool identity, target identity, provenance, diagnostics, and correspondence status
  + CFLP-023 bitstream signing, loading, rollback, revocation, and device authority are separate from procedure admission and remain absent until a target-specific SJS addendum
  + CFLP-024 model-generated HDL, HLS, constraints, or procedures may be candidates but can never self-verify, self-sign, self-load, or acquire device authority

& [ProofAndNonGoals] are conservative
  + a future proof must compare interpreter, software-native, HDL simulation, and hardware traces where those backends exist
  + side-channel, multi-tenant isolation, secure boot, partial reconfiguration, cryptographic key custody, and physical fault tolerance require target-specific treatment
  + no vendor, language, FPGA family, board, toolchain, frequency, interface, performance, cost, or deployment commitment is selected now
  + no source translator, RTL, HLS, simulation, synthesis, bitstream, driver, board action, or hardware purchase is authorized now

& [ExplosionDisposition] is ready_for_non_executable_refinement
  + all twenty-four requirements may become a signed correspondence profile only after refinement, constraints, justification, matrix, registry, and phase lock
  + any executable FPGA frontier requires a later target-specific preserved source and signature
